     * (NSEC3) semantics.
     *
     * Documented: Available from cPanel & WHM 86 (x-cpanel-available-version).
     *
     * Documented: This function configures the domain to use [Next Secure Record](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4470)
     * (NSEC) semantics instead of [Next Secure Record 3](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4470) (NSEC3) semantics.
     * **Note:** Only servers that run PowerDNS can use DNSSEC. If you call this function on a server that doesn't use
     * PowerDNS, you will receive an error.
     *
     * Documented: Inspect each domain disabled/error result separately from WHM metadata. NSEC semantics replace NSEC3;
     * the API result does not establish DNSSEC validation or propagation.
     *
     * API-map identity: whm1:unset_nsec3_for_domains#GET (wire name unset_nsec3_for_domains; Domain Management).
     *
     * @param string $domain The domain for which to disable NSEC3 semantics and use NSEC semantics.
     * @return UnsetNsec3ForDomainsResult
     * @throws ApiException If transport, HTTP, the API envelope outcome, or payload validation fails.
     * @throws PayloadMismatchException If the API envelope reported success but the payload differs from the contract;
     *     the operation may already have changed state; do not retry automatically.
     * @see https://api.docs.cpanel.net/specifications/whm.openapi/domain-management/dns-unset_nsec3_for_domains
     */
    public function unsetNsec3ForDomains(string $domain): array
    {
        /** @var UnsetNsec3ForDomainsResult $result Validated against DnsSpec::UNSET_NSEC3_FOR_DOMAINS. */
        $result = ($this->run)(DnsSpec::UNSET_NSEC3_FOR_DOMAINS, ['domain' => $domain]);

        return $result;
    }

